# Summary of changes for run e9fab3ef-f212-4c26-8f60-468910d67449
This research cycle developed the combinatorial and Hodge-theoretic core of the "Hodge conjecture for ReLU neural networks", starting from a cold start (the referenced files did not yet exist). All results compile with **0 sorries** and use only the standard axioms `propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound`.

**New files (under `Catalog/Bridges/`):**

1. `NeuralHodgeConjecture.lean` — the combinatorial backbone, built on the Zaslavsky budget `regionBound m n = Σ_{i≤n} C(m,i)`:
   - `regionBound_recurrence` (Pascal-type depth refinement), `regionBound_le_two_pow`, `regionBound_eq_two_pow` (dimensional saturation), `regionBound_mono_width`;
   - `regionBound_unique` — the binomial-sum formula is the *unique* solution of the depth-refinement recurrence with the two boundary rows (Conjecture 3), proved by double induction;
   - `regionBound_submultiplicative` and `regionBound_submultiplicative_eq` — the Künneth sub-multiplicativity law via Vandermonde, with equality once `a+b ≤ n` (Conjecture 2);
   - `reluHodge_totalBetti(_factor)`, `reluBetti_ceiling`, `reluBetti_saturation` — the saturated total Betti number `2^{w₁}·2^{wL}·mid` and its sharp ceiling/attainment (Conjecture 1);
   - `pl_hodge_span` / `pl_hodge_decomposition` — the "existence half": every PL chain is a unique integer combination of hyperplane sections.

2. `NeuralHodgeCatalogLink.lean` — the bridge to the existing catalog file `HodgeEPolynomial.lean` (`HodgeDiamond`):
   - `eulerChar_abs_le_totalDim` — `|χ(X)| ≤ totalDim(X)` for any nonnegative Hodge diamond (Conjecture 4), via a double triangle inequality;
   - `reluHodgeDiamond` (a concrete `HodgeDiamond` with `h^{p,q} = mid·C(w₁,p)·C(wL,q)`), with `reluHodgeDiamond_totalDim_eq` (catalog avatar of the total Betti number) and `reluHodgeDiamond_eulerChar_eq_zero` (Euler-triviality when a width is positive, from the vanishing alternating binomial sum).

Both files contain `-- !-- Lab Notes -- !--` blocks documenting the Hypothesis/Experiment/Analysis/Critique/Synthesis loop.

**Supporting deliverables:** `Catalog/Bridges/FUTURE_DIRECTIONS.md` (5 bold, falsifiable conjectures, each with a "The key insight is…" sentence and a "Why now?" justification, derived from this cycle) and `Catalog/Bridges/ComputationalEvidence.md` (small-case tables, counterexample hunt, OEIS notes).

**Build fix:** the project's `lakefile.toml` was missing `srcDir = "Catalog"`, without which none of the `import Bridges.X`-style modules (used throughout the existing project) could resolve; I added it so the project builds. All new modules build successfully via `lake build`.
